 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nNet interest income was $95.4B in FY2025 [1].\nNet interest income CAGR was +8.4% over FY2016..FY2025 [2].\nNet income was $57.0B in FY2025 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nNet interest income growth in FY2025 was +3.1% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2025 was -2.6% [3] [5].\nIn FY2025, net income growth of -2.6% [3] [5] was below net interest income growth of +3.1% [1] [4].\n\n## Margins\nNot enough data is available for this section in the selected periods.\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow of -$147.8B [6] was below net income of $57.0B [3].\nCash & equivalents was $343.3B in FY2025 [7].\nShareholders' equity was $362.4B in FY2025 [8].\n\n## Red flags\nNet interest income YoY growth decelerated across its three most recent measurable observations: +33.8% \u2192 +3.7% \u2192 +3.1%. Source operands: Net interest income USD 89,267,000,000 in FY2023 [9]; Net interest income USD 66,710,000,000 in FY2022 [10]; Net interest income USD 92,583,000,000 in FY2024 [4]; Net interest income USD 95,443,000,000 in FY2025 [1].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether net interest income growth in the next reporting update improves from +3.1% in FY2025 [1] [4].\nWatch how net income in the next reporting update compares with $57.0B in FY2025 [3].",
